Change(genesis='e30427e699992327267add669c3bc989f6d16525ba6f493121eec7778638e0ce', deps=('58633dfb6fffa68252b3b9759b53e20242702c36da54bb7adb03ed5bb8337397',), event=Authored(todo='typedtooling', at=datetime(2026, 11, 21, 5, 1, 35, 912028), actor='bmabsout', kind='todo', created=datetime(2026, 11, 19, 0, 0, 0), body="The merge train stops being a shell program: it is ported to a small typed Rust tool in four stages (the verdict table, publication, the gate run and its stop path, then build, land and record), each stage deleting the shell it replaces. The merge gate follows only if the train's port meets its bar: fewer guards, a faster run, and no growth in what a contributor must read.", spec=Flat(value=0.68), rationale=("A stop path's race in a shell trap could hang a train for hours, and the", 'two scripts need about two lines of test for each of their own.'), category='', waiting_on='', detail='In work on 2026-11-20: stages one and two have landed; stage three, the gate run and its stop path, is being written; stage four follows.\n\nState on 2026-11-21: stage three stopped on 2026-11-20 at its measured growth of the reading set (about ten times its projection, the ratio of the first two stages) and waited a day for an answer. Answered: the growth stands, since a train half in shell is the state the plan rules out; two holes of its stop path are closed in it (a push started and then stopped leaves no branch; the row written after the unlock is stated). The clause that the four stages must not grow the reading set has failed, so the port of the gate script does not happen. The last stage states its projected growth first, and takes over setting the context ratchet line when the train merges a change.', source=None, subtodos=(), notes=(), note=''))